# no-deferral.waivers — the committed allowlist for scripts/no-deferral-gate.sh.
#
# FORMAT:  <MATCHER><whitespace><reason> [retires: <TRACKER-ID>]
#   MATCHER is either an EXACT `path:line`, or a PATH GLOB (any matcher with no trailing `:<digits>`).
#   A marker (file:line) is WAIVED when an exact row equals it, or a glob row matches its file.
#   Every row must end in `[retires: <ID>]` naming the row of docs/design/1.6.0-TRACKER.md that
#   retires it. A row with no such tag, or one naming a tracker row that does not exist, is RED.
# The allowlist is a FLOOR CHECKED BOTH WAYS: a marker not waived is RED (over-count); a waiver that
# matches no marker is RED (stale — the marker was resolved). See scripts/no-deferral-gate.sh header
# and docs/design/playbook/gate-no-deferral.md.
#
# --strict-done (what scripts/verify-1.6.0-done.sh runs) additionally FAILS if ANY row below is not a
# */hot/* row: the hot/* foundation fixtures are the ONE permanent exemption; the voice skeleton rows
# are TRACKED 1.6.0 debt that MUST be gone before 1.6.0 is done.
#
# ── ONE GLOB USED TO STAND HERE, AND IT WAIVED WHATEVER APPEARED ─────────────────────────────────
# The single row `crates/busbar-plugin/src/hot/*` covered all 52 markers, never expired, and matched
# every marker any future edit put anywhere under that tree. The stale-waiver check could not fire on
# it either: one glob matching 52 markers stays "used" until the last one goes, so 51 could be
# resolved and the row would still look live. It was, in effect, a permanent unreviewed exemption for
# a whole directory.
#
# So the markers are enumerated one per line, each naming the slot it exempts and the tracker row
# that retires it. This costs a line-number edit whenever these files move — which is the point: the
# gate's stale-waiver check then reports exactly which exemptions no longer describe the tree,
# instead of a glob absorbing the change in silence.
#
# ── PERMANENT-UNTIL-H5: the plane-ABI foundation compile-surface fixtures ──────────────────────────
# `mod stub` / PlaneHostVtable::STUB / PlaneDecl::STUB. ADDITIVE and UNUSED — nothing in the engine
# calls them (hot/mod.rs); a STUB vtable slot panics BY DESIGN. They type-check that every extern
# "C-unwind" ABI fn-pointer slot has a real, well-typed signature. Their real hosts are the
# protocols-as-plugins effort (docs/design/1.6.0-protocols-as-plugins.md), tracked as H5.
#
# ── busbar-voice: the SKELETON / "dev-only until DoD" markers are CLEARED ───────────────────────────
# The voice plane's IR + both dialect codecs + T2 runtime + both topologies are implemented (behind the
# "runtime" feature) and the plane is installed at boot behind `plane-voice`; the stale SKELETON /
# "dev-only until DoD" marker prose in busbar-voice src has been reworded to truthful current-state, so
# no waiver rows remain for it. (Any residual "dev-only until DoD" prose outside busbar-voice src — e.g.
# the config-schema tracking note or the composition-root feature comment — is separate work.)

crates/busbar-plugin/src/hot/decl.rs:227	class-B label on the STUB doc comment that names the slots above; it documents the fixture, it is not a deferred capability [retires: H5]
